WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.000
It is the test on British life, history and customs that you need to apply for permanent residence (settlement / ILR) or British citizenship. 24 questions in 45 minutes. You pass with 75% or more.

2
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:29.700
It costs £50 and is booked online at least 3 days in advance. The questions come only from the official book «Life in the United Kingdom: A Guide for New Residents».

3
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:45.300
Bring the SAME identity document you booked with, the original (a photo is not accepted). If you have an eVisa, a share code is used. The name on the booking must match the document exactly.

4
00:00:45.300 --> 00:01:01.300
If you do not bring the right document, you cannot take the test and you do not get your money back. Under-18s and people aged 65 or over, among others, do not have to take it. If you fail, you can retake it as many times as you like, paying for each attempt.

5
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:08.500
Now do the lesson exercises. If you are unsure, watch this video again.
